  "prefLabel": "Ins 3101.01 Purpose",
  "priorExpiration": "2007-03-26",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 3101.01 Purpose. The purpose of this part is to require insurers, advisory organizations, nonprofit service organizations, health maintenance organizations, fraternal benefit societies, or their authorized filing agent(s) or representative(s), to submit all rates, forms, rule submissions or filings, and all applicable fees to the insurance department using the NAIC system for electronic rate and form filing (SERFF).\n\nSource. #5651, eff 7-1-93; ss by #6968, eff 3-26-99, EXPIRED: 3-26-07\n\nNew. #9282, eff 10-1-08; ss by #11147, eff 10-1-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins3100.html"
